Z||000000||engine18||03-10-2000||12:23 AM||||I'm in the process of removing my dash and replacing it with dash with no lower vent damage due to knees.  Does anyone in the forum have any wisdom in removing the dash.  Haynes publication doesn't have information on the removal and info from previous forum subject states that the procedure require as least 4 hours for one forum member to complete, but no insight on possible problems!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||chris6878||03-10-2000||12:38 AM||||any ideas how to fix the cracks on the dash? Mine has same cracks on the corners due to the knees....  <BR>TIA<BR>chris<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Carrolles||03-10-2000||12:41 AM||||I pulled the dash out of a wreck at a salvage yard to get to the wiring harness.  I got it out in about 1/2 hour.<P>If I recall correctly there are a few screws under the speaker grills on top of the dash.  You'll also have to remove the instrument cluster.  Be sure and remove all the screws holding it in.  There are a couple down behind the cluster on top of the steering column.  If you yank on the cluster without getting these screws you will damage the printed circuit board of the instrument cluster (speaking from experience on a junker.  Cluster was trashed already though).  I believe there are a few screws at the lower edge of the dash pad also.  It's been a while and I was in a real hurry (did it on lunch break).<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll ||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||03-10-2000||12:53 AM||||  If you want info on dash retraction you might want to contact EARNE(member) He replaced his dash with the tightest PISA leather dash ever. I'm sure he would have some tips. Also see his pics in the Monkeyman pics post. Cool; VERY Cool!!!!!<P><BR> Late, Bam out <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||03-10-2000||12:58 AM||||   Sorry, That would be in the General Fiero Chat area. Awsome pics, Bad GT!!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000005||Monkeyman||03-10-2000||05:50 AM||||There's a little more to it than that.  If Earne can't help you, email me and I'll walk you through it.  I just gutted the interior of the Monkeymobile (with the intention of saving as much as I could so I didn't just tear everything out.).||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||03-10-2000||07:47 AM||||FieroDave has a way to repair those damaged dash corners using a kind of epoxy stick putty. Check the search function to find that topic or email him.||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||10:15 AM||||I also have been told a way to fix the dash corners using fibreglass resin and tissues.  This was told to me by Mr. David Rodabaugh.  He claims that the resultant texture is very similar to the original grainy texture of the dash. <P>Hope this helps,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
